# Misinformation and AI

#### One of the most common ways these ethical questions show up in the classroom is through misinformation.

#### AI are capable of producing responses that sound clear, confident, and highly convincing. However, these responses are not always accurate. In some cases, AI systems generate information that is incorrect, misleading, or entirely fabricated.

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>AI Fictions or Fabrications:</strong> content that AI systems generate that is incorrect or misleading.</p>
</div>

#### AI fiction occurs because large language models like ChatGPT or Gemini do not actually understand the content they produce. Instead, they generate responses by predicting the most likely sequence of words based on patterns learned from large amounts of text.

#### Because of this, AI can fill in gaps, make assumptions, or generate details that are inaccurate. While responses may sound confident and complete, they are not verified for accuracy.

<p style="text-align:center;"><img src="https://images.code.org/b345e75edd30dcf95dcf431466604d55-AI-Its-going-to-rain.jpg" alt="alt text"></p>

*Image: Convert 2026*

#### Check out Module 2, Understanding AI to learn more about how AI works and why AI generates misinformation.

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 You may also hear the term “<strong>hallucinations</strong>” used to describe this phenomenon. <br><br>While it is commonly used in discussions about AI, some educators and researchers choose not to use this term because it can imply human-like thinking or perception. <br><br>Instead, terms like AI fiction or fabricated content more accurately reflect what is happening: the system is generating plausible-sounding language without understanding or verifying its accuracy.</p>
</div>

#### Understanding AI fiction is a key part of using AI responsibly. It requires healthy skepticism, careful verification, and the ability to question what you see.
